# Staging host settings (#50): the template for ~/tarubot/.env on the staging host, which runs
# DevBot's application under the staging tool-guard profile, against its own database and role on
# the shared managed cluster. Fill in a copy with staging-only values, never from a production
# copy, keep it outside any checkout (mode 600), and send it over SSH stdin:
#   ssh tarubot@<staging host> 'umask 077; cat > ~/tarubot/.env' < staging.env
# Refresh the encrypted settings copy after every change (docs/HOSTING.md, "Settings copy").
#
# Not set here: the staging target (ops/quadlet/staging/target.env) fixes DevBot's application ID,
# TARUBOT_ENVIRONMENT=staging, DevBot's test guild and public test replies, whatever this file says.
# Staging never holds the GitHub App settings: /suggest posts publicly, and the playbook refuses any
# GITHUB_APP_* value on staging. The optional tunables (LOG_LEVEL, the intervals, LODESTONE_*,
# GITHUB_REPORTS_REPO) are left out, so the bot's defaults apply; add one only with a value, because
# ops/quadlet/check-env.sh refuses an empty one.
#
# systemd and Compose must read every line the same way, so check-env.sh --syntax refuses a $ or a
# backslash in a value, inline comments and export lines. Percent-encode such characters in the URL.
#
# This file stays the only place the secrets are kept. Before every start, ops/quadlet/secrets.sh
# copies all six secrets from it into the Podman secrets the bot reads as files: DATABASE_URL,
# DATABASE_CA_CERT, DISCORD_TOKEN, GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY, GITHUB_REPORTS_TOKEN and
# HEALTHCHECKS_PING_URL. It refuses to start with any of the first three empty. The GitHub App key,
# always empty on staging, is copied as an empty secret but never mounted: only production's
# target mounts it. The unit sets each NAME_FILE itself, so add none here.

# The release this host runs: exactly one plain line, which deploys rewrite.
TARUBOT_IMAGE_TAG=REPLACE_WITH_RELEASE_VERSION
# Staging's own database and role, both tarubot_staging, on the managed cluster's direct port 27520
# (never the 27521 pool). The staging profile refuses production's tarubot and tarubot_restore.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://tarubot_staging:REPLACE_WITH_STAGING_PASSWORD@REPLACE_WITH_CLUSTER_HOST:27520/tarubot_staging
# The managed cluster's CA certificate, quoted across lines.
DATABASE_CA_CERT="-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
REPLACE_WITH_MANAGED_CLUSTER_CA_CERTIFICATE
-----END CERTIFICATE-----"
# Keep this obvious placeholder until the DevBot move: the owner resets DevBot's token then, and
# the new token goes only here. The bot never starts on staging before the move.
DISCORD_TOKEN=REPLACE_AT_THE_DEVBOT_MOVE
# The test guild's #chat channel for the startup test plan; empty looks for #chat by name.
TEST_PLAN_CHANNEL_ID=
# Staging's own fine-grained token, with issues write on the private reports repository only,
# because staging runs PR code. Empty keeps reports in the database, unsent.
GITHUB_REPORTS_TOKEN=
# A staging heartbeat check without alerts, or empty to turn the heartbeat off. Never production's.
HEALTHCHECKS_PING_URL=
# ops/backup.sh: staging's own bucket and access key, limited to that bucket, and its own backup
# check. Never production's. The bot never sees these settings.
BACKUP_STORAGE_ENDPOINT=
BACKUP_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY=
BACKUP_STORAGE_SECRET_KEY=
BACKUP_STORAGE_REGION=
HEALTHCHECKS_BACKUP_URL=
